<title>SPAIN: Spain's La Caixa H1 attributable net 27.34 pct up.</title>
<headline>Spain's La Caixa H1 attributable net 27.34 pct up.</headline>
<dateline>MADRID 1997-07-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Spanish Catalonia's saving bank La Caixa announced on Wednesday the following first-half results. (billion pesetas, unless stated)</p>
<p>						  H1 97     H1 96</p>
<p> Net attributable profit		 42.61  vs   33.46</p>
<p> Net profit				  46.36  vs   37.38</p>
<p> Pretax profit			     65.73  vs   51.52</p>
<p> Net interest income		    122.28  vs  115.20</p>
<p> Ordinary income			  171.66  vs  152.07</p>
<p> Operating income			  50.96  vs   39.71</p>
<p> Interest revenue			 353.77  vs   415.19</p>
<p> Interest expenses			231.49  vs   300.00</p>
<p> Fees and commissions		    43.97  vs    33.98</p>
<p> Financial/trading rev		    5.40  vs     2.89</p>
<p> Operating costs			  120.70  vs   112.36</p>
<p>    -personnel costs		     72.69  vs    68.79</p>
<p>    -general, administrative costs   34.08  vs    32.54</p>
<p>    - depreciation			 13.93  vs    11.03</p>
<p>Net earnings from equity-accounted</p>
<p>    holdings				 25.34  vs    20.74</p>
<p> Net loan-loss provisions		 7.97  vs     9.04</p>
<p>-- Madrid newsroom + 34 1 585 8340</p>
</text>
